# The generator measures page size in memory and the build fails anything over
# 17,999 bytes. If a template arrived with CRLF the count would shift under the
# guard, so line endings are normalised in the repository rather than left to
# each contributor's core.autocrlf.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.png binary
*.zip binary

# Captured fixtures are byte-for-byte records of what a firewall served, and
# their measured sizes are quoted in docs/architecture/ -- the login prefix is
# 8,394 B, and the custom content begins at exactly that offset. Normalising
# line endings or trimming whitespace would change those numbers and make the
# spliced preview diverge from the page it reproduces. Treat them as binary so
# nothing rewrites them.
src/panos_response_pages/data/fixtures/** -text
